# Repository instructions

## Layout

- Laboratory configuration: `opensdl.yaml`
- Workflows: `workflows/`
- Organization code: `src/{{ package }}/`
- Local adapters: `src/{{ package }}/adapters/`
- Organization domain models: `src/{{ package }}/domain/`
- Tests: `tests/`

## Required checks

- `uv run opensdl validate opensdl.yaml --workflow workflows/first-run.yaml`
- `uv run opensdl doctor --manifest opensdl.yaml`
- `uv run pytest`

## Working state

- Start fresh work with `git status --short`, the `orient-lab` skill, and the selected manifest.
- Resume work by refreshing Git, tests, and the selected manifest. Query runtime evidence only when
  the task requires it, account for query side effects, and preserve unrelated changes and setup.
- Git records intended implementation. `.opensdl/` records local execution state and stays out of
  Git. Conversation history is private context.
- The active harness controls local permissions. The manifest, policy, and runtime control
  laboratory actions.

Repository skills live in `.agents/skills/`. Keep credentials, live endpoints, sensitive facility
details, and generated run state out of Git. Implement changes with tests and configuration.
